## Summary

All five checklist items (CHK-0066 through CHK-0070) are classified as **not-a-vulnerability**. The core finding is that BLS field element range validation is entirely and correctly delegated to the C-KZG-4844 library (v2.1.1), which provides a single canonical implementation of `bytes_to_bls_field()` in `/home/gohan/go/pkg/mod/github.com/ethereum/c-kzg-4844/v2@v2.1.1/src/common/bytes.c` (lines 64-70).

Key architectural guarantees:

1. **Proposer path (CHK-0066)**: Every blob bytes-to-cells conversion goes through `ComputeCells()` → C `blob_to_polynomial()` → `bytes_to_bls_field()` per field element. For Fulu blocks, `validateBlobs()` in `handlers.go:1090` calls `VerifyCellKZGProofBatchFromBlobData()` which calls `ComputeCells()` before any KZG arithmetic.

2. **Validator path (CHK-0067)**: `verify_cell_kzg_proof_batch()` in the C library calls `bytes_to_bls_field()` at `eip7594.c:666` for every cell field element inside `compute_commitment_to_aggregated_interpolation_poly()`. Out-of-range elements return `C_KZG_BADARGS` which propagates correctly to `ValidationReject`.

3. **Falsification (CHK-0068)**: Definitively disproved. `bytes_to_bls_field()` is called unconditionally within `verify_cell_kzg_proof_batch()` before the final pairing check. `*ok=true` is unreachable when any field element is out of range.

4. **Implementation consistency (CHK-0069)**: There is only ONE implementation of `bytes_to_bls_field` in the entire codebase. All usages are consistent: big-endian byte ordering, same BLS_MODULUS constant (a BLST compile-time constant), proper error propagation.

5. **Downstream protection (CHK-0070)**: The 'goto out' pattern in the C library correctly aborts all downstream cryptographic operations (polynomial aggregation, commitment weighting, proof linear combination, pairing verification) when `bytes_to_bls_field()` fails. `*ok` is initialized to false and only set to true by `pairings_verify()`, which is unreachable after an error.

